    <node id="concept_atlas">
      <data key="d1">The Atlas of Worlds (concept)</data>
      <data key="d2">["Atlas", "Atlas of Worlds"]</data>
      <data key="d3">concept</data>
      <data key="d24" />
      <data key="d4">The endgame structure of PoE1: a web of alternate worlds ('maps') reached through the Map Device. Wiki lore says it was either found or created by the Elder as a hunting ground; after the Elder's defeat other powers (Maven, Eldritch Horrors, the Originator) contest it. PoE2 has its own, separate Atlas whose Precursor Towers are mentioned in PoE1 wiki lore.</data>
      <data key="d5">["poe1", "poe2"]</data>
      <data key="d6">endgame_plot</data>
      <data key="d7">[]</data>
      <data key="d8">poe1_atlas</data>
      <data key="d9">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": null, "story_order": null}</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">canon</data>
      <data key="d12">medium</data>
      <data key="d13">[{"source_id": "src_poewiki_history_of_wraeclast", "locator": "section 'The Atlas of Worlds' / 'The Elder and the Shaper'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_the_decay", "locator": "lead: 'The Atlas of Worlds may have originally been created as a feeding ground for the Elder'"}]</data>
      <data key="d14">["poe1_atlas"]</data>
      <data key="d15">["poe1_atlas"]</data>
      <data key="d16">["endgame_plot"]</data>
      <data key="d18">released</data>
      <data key="d19">8</data>
      <data key="d20">2</data>
