    <node id="concept_cataclysm">
      <data key="d1">Cataclysm</data>
      <data key="d2">[]</data>
      <data key="d3">concept</data>
      <data key="d24">recurring_catastrophe</data>
      <data key="d4">Lore term for the world-ending catastrophes that destroyed civilisations: the unknown cataclysm that wiped out the Precursors, the Vaal Cataclysm (also 'The Fall', c. 400 BIC), and the Eternal Empire Cataclysm (~1339 IC). The corpus uses the word for each event but does not define a single in-world category; this node groups those uses. Not the PoE2 epilogue quest 'Cataclysm's Wake', which is an Atlas tutorial quest.</data>
      <data key="d5">["poe1", "poe2"]</data>
      <data key="d6">background</data>
      <data key="d7">[]</data>
      <data key="d8">vaal</data>
      <data key="d9">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": "from the Precursor era to c. 1339 IC (several events)", "story_order": null}</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">canon</data>
      <data key="d12">medium</data>
      <data key="d13">[{"source_id": "src_poewiki_history_of_wraeclast", "locator": "intro: 'An incredibly advanced precursor civilization existed, but was wiped out by an unknown cataclysm.'; section '====The Vaal Cataclysm====': 'The Vaal Cataclysm, also known as The Fall, was a historical event...'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_eternal_empire", "locator": "section '===The Cataclysm (~1339 IC)===': 'The Cataclysm brought an end to Voll's reign and the Eternal Empire as a whole.'"}, {"source_id": "src_poe2wiki_cataclysm_s_wake", "locator": "page intro: 'Cataclysm's Wake is an epilogue quest. It act as the tutorial quest for the Atlas.'"}]</data>
      <data key="d14">["gap_deep_history_vaal_precursor_eternal"]</data>
