    <node id="concept_corruption">
      <data key="d1">Corruption</data>
      <data key="d2">[]</data>
      <data key="d3">concept</data>
      <data key="d24">lore_force</data>
      <data key="d4">Lore force of mutation and malformation tied to the Beast and its predecessors: the Beast 'possesses corrupting powers' that mutate whatever contacts it; Kitava is called 'God of Corruption' in Karui dialogue; Precursors mastered corruption and Doryani attempts to harness the Precursor Weapon to destroy corruption. Not the Corrupted-item mechanic.</data>
      <data key="d5">["poe1", "poe2"]</data>
      <data key="d6">background</data>
      <data key="d7">[]</data>
      <data key="d8">primordial</data>
      <data key="d9">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": "from the Precursor era onward (Beast, Vaal, Eternal Empire)", "story_order": null}</data>
      <data key="d10">[]</data>
      <data key="d11">canon</data>
      <data key="d12">medium</data>
      <data key="d13">[{"source_id": "src_poewiki_the_beast_lore", "locator": "intro: 'The Beast possesses corrupting powers, devouring the souls of his prey and mutating whoever comes in contact with it.'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_karui_gods", "locator": "section '==Kitava==' &gt; Dialogue, Haku's 'Kaom' option: 'Kitava, God of Corruption, consumed Kaom from heart to skin.'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_history_of_wraeclast", "locator": "section '===Precursor civilization===': 'After mastering corruption, they delved deeper...'; the Precursor Weapon is one 'which Doryani attempts to harness to destroy corruption'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_karui_gods", "locator": "Haku dialogue: 'Kitava, God of Corruption'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_sin", "locator": "PoE2 section: 'the Seed of Corruption'"}, {"source_id": "src_poewiki_history_of_wraeclast", "locator": "Vaal temple section: 'worship of Corruption'"}]</data>
      <data key="d14">["gap_deep_history_vaal_precursor_eternal", "gap_isolated_links"]</data>
      <data key="d15">["primordial"]</data>
      <data key="d16">["background"]</data>
      <data key="d25">[{"domain": "gap_isolated_links", "summary": "The in-world corrupting power named by the Karui and Vaal (Kitava as 'God of Corruption', worship of Corruption at a Vaal temple) and carried as the Seed of Corruption (what remains of the Beast) in PoE2. The item-corruption mechanic is a separate game system."}]</data>
      <data key="d18">released</data>
      <data key="d19">15</data>
      <data key="d20">2</data>
