    <node id="concept_exile">
      <data key="d1">Exile (exile system)</data>
      <data key="d2">["Exiled to Wraeclast"]</data>
      <data key="d3">concept</data>
      <data key="d24">exile_practice</data>
      <data key="d4">The exile system: criminals of Oriath are sentenced by the Templar government and shipped to Wraeclast. The sentence text reads 'You are hereby Exiled to Wraeclast where, it is hoped, you shall come to repent your Sins'. The player's character is one of these exiles. Precedent exists: under Tyndarus Phrecius, people were exiled to the land later called Trarthus. The wiki gives no single in-world reason for choosing Wraeclast.</data>
      <data key="d5">["poe1", "poe2"]</data>
      <data key="d6">main_plot</data>
      <data key="d7">[]</data>
      <data key="d8">poe1_campaign</data>
      <data key="d9">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": "1599-1600 IC (PoE1); Trarthus precedent c. 870 IC", "story_order": null}</data>
