    <node id="event_searing_exarch_quest">
      <data key="d1">The Searing Exarch (quest)</data>
      <data key="d2">[]</data>
      <data key="d3">event</data>
      <data key="d24">quest</data>
      <data key="d4">Epilogue quest added in 3.17.0 and run in parallel with The Maven and The Eater of Worlds quests. The Envoy gives the Luminous Astrolabe, which lets the Exile add Searing Exarch influence to Tier 9 to 16 maps. The Tier 11 map boss drops a Polaric Invitation to the Black Star's arena (area level 79); the Tier 16 map boss drops an Incandescent Invitation to the Searing Exarch's arena (The Absence of Patience and Wisdom). The Black Star is defeated first, then the Searing Exarch. The quest pays out Atlas passive points (2 skill points, 4 respec points on completion) and an Omniscient Voidstone via Kirac; the Exarch drops an Eldritch Voidstone if The Eater of Worlds was defeated first.</data>
      <data key="d5">["poe1"]</data>
      <data key="d6">endgame_plot</data>
      <data key="d7">[]</data>
      <data key="d8">poe1_atlas</data>
      <data key="d9">{"in_world_year": null, "relative": "PoE1 endgame (3.17.0 Siege of the Atlas)", "story_order": 3082, "parallel_group": "atlas_pinnacle_quests"}</data>
      <data key="d10">["act_poe1_epilogue"]</data>
      <data key="d11">canon</data>
      <data key="d12">medium</data>
      <data key="d13">[{"source_id": "src_poewiki_the_searing_exarch_quest", "locator": "infobox (boss The Searing Exarch) and Walkthrough: quest intro 'This quest runs in parallel to The Maven (quest) and The Eater of Worlds (quest)'; 'Use the Luminous Astrolabe', 'Polaric Invitation', 'Incandescent Invitation' steps; Quest Complete log 'You have gained 2 Atlas Passive Skill Points and 4 Atlas Passive Respec Points'; version history 3.17.0"}]</data>
      <data key="d14">["gap_atlas_endgame_poe1_poe2"]</data>
      <data key="d15">["poe1_atlas"]</data>
